// A node sits as close to what it names as its placements allow, in every
// direction.
//
// "left of" and "above" bound their target rather than the node that wrote
// them, so a node carrying only those has nothing behind it pushing it toward
// what it names. It used to settle at the far edge of the drawing instead,
// which was neither what the file said nor what the language promises.
//
// "near" is carried rightward by the chain from the anchor, and the note has to
// follow it. The note's right edge belongs one tight gap from "near", wherever
// that ends up. Widen a label anywhere in the chain and it still does.
//
// The benchmark cannot show this: every note in it is bounded on both sides or
// placed with "right of", so nothing there drifts. This file is the coverage.

box anchor "anchor"
box far    "far"   right of anchor
box near   "near"  right of far

note trailing "one tight gap from near"  left of near  below anchor  gap: tight  overlap: allow
